omimetic amines—can cause acute hypertensive emergencies when co-administered with MAO inhibitors. The underlying mechanism involves massive release of stored norepinephrine due to MAO inhibition, which is exacerbated by these agents’ ability to displace catecholamines from neuronal vesicles. Clinical evidence explicitly warns that combinations like MAOIs with 阿拉明 or 麻黄素 may result in fatal outcomes, including cerebral hemorrhage or coma. [Data: Relationships (31394, 28971, 12180); Entities (9096, 9462, 9011, 5746, 10415)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"异丙肼 is linked to multiple severe adverse reactions\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The MAOI drug 异丙肼 (iproniazid) is associated with serious adverse effects, particularly 血压过度升高 (excessive blood pressure elevation), when combined with tyramine-rich substances like 酰鱼 and 酒类. Evidence indicates that consumption of these foods during 异丙肼 therapy can trigger dangerous hypertensive episodes due to impaired tyramine metabolism. Additionally, 异丙肼’s classification within the MAOI class places it at the center of numerous high-risk drug-food and drug-drug interactions documented in this community. [Data: Relationships (37872, 37874, 11748); Entities (5425, 12850, 12839, 17310)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"痢特灵 induces disulfiram-like reactions with alcohol\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The antimicrobial drug 痢特灵 (furazolidone) is known to cause disulfiram-like reactions upon exposure to ethanol. This reaction results from inhibition of aldehyde dehydrogenase, leading to acetaldehyde accumulation and symptoms such as facial flushing, tachycardia, nausea, hypotension, and in severe cases, shock or arrhythmias. Although not directly part of the MAOI core, 痢特灵 shares mechanistic overlap as it also exhibits MAO-inhibiting properties, thereby contributing to the broader risk profile of this pharmacological network. [Data: Relationships (14358); Entities (7100)]\"\n        },\n 