mplified under general anesthesia. These findings emphasize the need for careful patient selection and monitoring. [Data: Relationships (16731, 12180); Entities (9011, 5746)]\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 8.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The community poses high clinical impact due to multiple documented pathways leading to life-threatening hypertensive crises, arrhythmias, and other severe adverse reactions from common drug-food and drug-drug combinations.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "created": 1782126675, "model": "qwen3-max", "object": "chat.completion", "moderation": null, "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1578, "prompt_tokens": 6852, "total_tokens": 8430, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 1408}}, "formatted_response": null, "content": "{\n    \"title\": \"MAO Inhibitor-Related Drug and Food Interaction Network\",\n    \"summary\": \"This community centers around monoamine oxidase (MAO) inhibitors and their interactions with various drugs, food items, and associated adverse effects. Key entities include the drug class '单氨氧化酶抑制剂' (monoamine oxidase inhibitors), specific drugs such as 异丙肼, 阿拉明, 麻黄素, 间羟胺, 新福林, 痢特灵, and优降灵, as well as foods like 乳酪, 酰鱼, and 酒类. These entities are linked through documented pharmacological interactions that can lead to severe adverse reactions, including hypertensive crisis, arrhythmias, and disulfiram-like reactions. The network highlights significant clinical risks arising from concomitant use of MAO inhibitors with sympathomimetic agents or tyramine-rich foods.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"MAO inhibitors interact dangerously with tyramine-rich foods\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Monoamine oxidase 